member.param:
If this parameter is TRUE, the function creates a manual-reset event object, which requires the use of the ResetEvent
function to set the event state to nonsignaled. If this parameter is FALSE, the function creates an auto-reset event object,
and system automatically resets the event state to nonsignaled after a single waiting thread has been released.

member.summary:
Absolute new end-of-file position as a byte offset from the start of the file. EndOfFile specifies the byte offset to the
end of the file. Because this value is zero-based, it actually refers to the first free byte in the file. In other words,
EndOfFile is the offset to the byte immediately following the last valid byte in the file.

